beastie needs mbsync and msmtp configs before Pat can read and post
through lab-mail. They ship as samples in the notmuch package,
installed only where no config exists, so a host that has its own,
like lab-claude, keeps it.

- pat@p7x.dev may write the list, so mbsync syncs both ways and
  expunges on both sides, and Pat's moves reach lab-mail.
- The password comes from pass(1), so no secret is in the repo.
- README.org gives the commands to set up, sync, and post.
