@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+#+TITLE: dotfiles/notmuch
+
+notmuch hooks and configs for the lab-devel list. =just install=
+installs them as a package under =~=.
+
+* lab-mail
+The =lab-mail= profile reads the list as synced from lab-mail, whose
+spec is =../../jails/instances/lab-mail/spec.org=. On beastie, the
+package also installs =~/.mbsyncrc= and =~/.msmtprc= for pat@p7x.dev,
+if they do not exist.
+
+** set up
+Store the password of pat@p7x.dev on lab-mail in pass(1), and make the
+mail root with its =sent= folder, which is never synced. mbsync
+creates the list's folders:
+#+BEGIN_EXAMPLE
+pass insert lab-mail/pat@p7x.dev
+mkdir -p ~/mail/pat@p7x.dev/sent/cur ~/mail/pat@p7x.dev/sent/new \
+    ~/mail/pat@p7x.dev/sent/tmp
+just install
+#+END_EXAMPLE
+
+** sync and read
+Syncing and indexing are separate commands. mbsync syncs INBOX,
+=Next=, =Later=, and =Archive= with lab-mail, both ways, and notmuch
+indexes what it brought:
+#+BEGIN_EXAMPLE
+mbsync lab-mail && NOTMUCH_PROFILE=lab-mail notmuch new
+NOTMUCH_PROFILE=lab-mail notmuch search tag:inbox
+#+END_EXAMPLE
+
+To file a message, move its file to another folder's =cur/=, and
+drop the =,U== part of its name, so mbsync takes it for a new message
+there. The next sync moves it on lab-mail.
+
+** post
+msmtp posts as pat@p7x.dev. With =-t= it takes the recipients from
+the To, Cc, and Bcc headers:
+#+BEGIN_EXAMPLE
+msmtp -t < message.eml
+#+END_EXAMPLE
+
+lab-mail delivers mail for the list's addresses to the list, and
+accepts and discards mail for the people who read it. It refuses any
+other recipient, and msmtp then posts nothing and exits non-zero.
diff --git a/dotfiles/notmuch/lab-mail/mbsyncrc.sample b/dotfiles/notmuch/lab-mail/mbsyncrc.sample
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..ba3b32ca
--- /dev/null
+++ b/dotfiles/notmuch/lab-mail/mbsyncrc.sample
@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@
+# ~/.mbsyncrc: sync the list with lab-mail into ~/mail/pat@p7x.dev;
+# see mbsync(1). The package installs this as ~/.mbsyncrc only if that
+# file does not exist, and never overwrites it.
+#
+# pat@p7x.dev may change the list, so the sync runs both ways and
+# expunges on both sides: a move or deletion here takes effect on
+# lab-mail at the next run. Fastmail still keeps every message. Only
+# the list's folders are synced, and the folders come from lab-mail.
+#
+# lab-mail listens only on loopback, so there is no TLS. The password
+# is the one whose hash lab-mail keeps in imap-users.
+
+IMAPAccount lab-mail
+Host 127.0.0.1
+Port 2143
+TLSType None
+AuthMechs LOGIN
+User pat@p7x.dev
+PassCmd "pass show lab-mail/pat@p7x.dev"
+
+IMAPStore lab-mail
+Account lab-mail
+
+MaildirStore local
+Path ~/mail/pat@p7x.dev/
+Inbox ~/mail/pat@p7x.dev/INBOX
+
+Channel lab-mail
+Far :lab-mail:
+Near :local:
+Patterns INBOX Next Later Archive
+Create Near
+Sync All
+Expunge Both
+Remove None
+CopyArrivalDate yes
diff --git a/dotfiles/notmuch/lab-mail/msmtprc.sample b/dotfiles/notmuch/lab-mail/msmtprc.sample
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..e228ef96
--- /dev/null
+++ b/dotfiles/notmuch/lab-mail/msmtprc.sample
@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+# ~/.msmtprc: post to the list through lab-mail; see msmtp(1). The
+# package installs this as ~/.msmtprc only if that file does not
+# exist, and never overwrites it.
+#
+# lab-mail listens only on loopback and takes posts with no login, so
+# there is no auth and no TLS. msmtp exits non-zero if any recipient
+# is refused, and the message then goes to no one.
+
+defaults
+auth off
+tls off
+
+account lab-mail
+host 127.0.0.1
+port 2525
+from pat@p7x.dev
+
+account default : lab-mail
